P1c -- AIR-SEA dpCO2, MODEL vs OBSERVATION. ⛔ A COMPARISON, NOT A GATE. 
rulings: A1 (SH 0-90 S, the driver's own aggregation) is PRIMARY; A2 (40-90 S) is REFERENCE. 
quantity: dpCO2 = ocean pCO2 - atmospheric CO2, GATE S's own quantity (ruling B2). 
estimator: AREA-MEAN first, then ONE harmonic -- a well-mixed box has an area-mean 
           concentration, so a per-cell amplitude mean is the WRONG reduction. 
 
observed atmospheric SPO harmonic: amp 1.170 ppm, peak month 9.01 (n = 49 yr) 
 
running the model (spinup + 95 yr, R core, both arms) ... 
 
SH dpCO2 -- amplitude (uatm) and peak month 
                                            amp    peak mo 
  MODEL, seas_ml = 0                      20.57       6.24 
  MODEL, seas_ml = 1                      54.04       6.79 
  OBS A1 (0 to 90 S)  <- THE RULING        4.47       1.61 
  OBS A2 (40 to 90 S)  (reference)        15.46       7.39 
 
AGAINST THE RULED TARGET (A1, the whole SH ocean): 
  amplitude  model 54.04 vs obs 4.47  -> ratio 12.09 
  phase      model 6.79 vs obs 1.61  -> 5.18 months apart 
FOR REFERENCE ONLY (A2, GATE S's 40-90 S band): 
  amplitude  ratio 3.50 | phase 0.61 months apart 
 
⛔ NO VERDICT IS RETURNED. If the model sits close to A2 and far from A1, that is the 
   STRUCTURAL finding the ruling was expected to expose: a LOW-LATITUDE box (84 % of 
   the SH ocean) carrying a HIGH-LATITUDE seasonal cycle, because the MLD climatology 
   driving it is an SH-wide mean dominated by high-latitude winter mixing. It would 
   NOT be a falsification of entrainment. 
⚠ The two observed regimes are ANTIPHASE (subtropics peak Jan, Southern Ocean Jul-Aug), 
   so A1's amplitude is a 4.4x CANCELLATION of A2's and is fragile by construction. 
 
